<th id="S3.T1.4.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:3.5pt;padding-right:3.5pt;" colspan="5"><span id="S3.T1.4.7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Correlation with the Supercategory <math id="S3.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.T1.4.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (mean <math id="S3.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> std, detailed in Appx. <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Train-Test Split Design on Attribute Generalization (continued) ‣ Not All Splits Are Equal: Rethinking Attribute Generalization Across Unrelated Categories" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>)</span></span></th></tr>
