<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2509.06998v1/figures/correlation_random_split.png" id="A3.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/156;" width="234" height="156" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2509.06998v1/figures/correlation_k_means.png" id="A3.F2.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/156;" width="234" height="156" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>In <span id="A3.F2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Random</span> grouping (left), a positive correlation emerges, indicating reliance on supercategory-specific features. In contrast, the split based on <span id="A3.F2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Embedding Clustering</span> yields a near-zero correlation, suggesting improved generalization and reduced semantic leakage.</figcaption>
</figure>
